menu "Knob board"

    config KNOB_BOARD_INVERT
        bool "Invert knob direction"
        default n
        help
            Swap clockwise and anticlockwise. The knob's A contact is wired as
            clockwise on the Waveshare 1.8" module; set this only if a unit
            turns the wrong way.

    choice KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_MOTOR
        prompt "Haptic motor type"
        default KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_MOTOR_LRA
        help
            What the DRV2605L's OUT+/OUT- drive. The schematic labels them
            LRA_P / LRA_N, and on the board the motor only moves when driven
            as an LRA: in ERM mode (what Waveshare's demo selects) it gets a
            near-DC drive and barely stirs.

        config KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_MOTOR_LRA
            bool "LRA (linear resonant actuator) -- this board"
        config KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_MOTOR_ERM
            bool "ERM (eccentric rotating mass)"
    endchoice

    config KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_ROM_LIBRARY
        int "DRV2605 waveform library"
        range 1 7
        default 6 if KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_MOTOR_LRA
        default 5
        help
            6 is the LRA library; 1-5 are ERM libraries, 7 the 4.5 V ERM one.

    config KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_LRA_PERIOD
        int "LRA open-loop drive period (OL_LRA_PERIOD)"
        range 1 127
        default 51
        depends on KNOB_BOARD_HAPTIC_MOTOR_LRA
        help
            Open loop drives the LRA at 1 / (period x 98.46 us). 51 is the
            DRV2605L's reset value, about 199 Hz, inside the 170-235 Hz band
            small coin LRAs resonate in. Nudge it if the buzz feels weak:
            lower is a higher frequency.

endmenu
